# Selection & Actions

Registering even one [`DataTableAction`](/api-reference/index/interfaces/DataTableAction) lights up the entire selection UI: a leading checkbox column, a trailing three-dot per-row dropdown, and a bulk-action toolbar that slides in next to the search field when at least one row is selected. Selection persists across pagination, so cross-page bulk operations work without extra code.

## Registering actions

Each action needs a `key` (stable, lookup id for translated labels) plus either `onSingle`, `onMulti`, or both.

```typescript
import type { DataTableAction, DataTableConfig, SelectionId } from 'svelte-advanced-datatable';
import PencilIcon from './PencilIcon.svelte';
import ArchiveIcon from './ArchiveIcon.svelte';
import TrashIcon from './TrashIcon.svelte';

const config: DataTableConfig<UserData> = {
    type: 'userDataActions',
    columnProperties: { /* ... */ },
    dataUniquePropertyKey: 'id',
    actions: [
        {
            key: 'edit',
            icon: PencilIcon,
            onSingle: (item) => openEditDialog(item)
        },
        {
            key: 'archive',
            icon: ArchiveIcon,
            primary: true,
            onMulti: (ids) => archiveUsers(ids)
        },
        {
            key: 'delete',
            icon: TrashIcon,
            variant: 'destructive',
            primary: true,
            onMulti: (ids) => deleteUsers(ids)
        }
    ],
    messageConfig: {
        // ...column labels...
        actions: { edit: 'Edit', archive: 'Archive', delete: 'Delete' }
    }
};
```

`onMulti` receives **IDs only** — cross-page selections can include rows that aren't loaded in memory. Refetch with the IDs when the handler needs full objects.

When only `onMulti` is supplied, single-row invocations call it with `[id]`. That's the common case for destructive/bulk-shaped actions.

## Action properties

| Property               | Type                                  | Description                                                                                                                | Default                |
|:-----------------------|:--------------------------------------|:---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|:-----------------------|
| `key`                  | `string`                              | Stable id. Used as a list key and as the message-formatter lookup for the label.                                            | required               |
| `icon`                 | `Component`                           | Svelte icon component. Render an SVG sized via tailwind (e.g. `class="size-4"`).                                            | —                      |
| `variant`              | `'default' \| 'primary' \| 'destructive'` | Visual styling — destructive = red.                                                                                     | `'default'`            |
| `primary`              | `boolean`                             | Render as a standalone button in the bulk toolbar (otherwise lives in the "More" overflow). Capped by `primaryActionsCount`. | `false`                |
| `hideInRow`            | `boolean`                             | Suppress in the per-row dropdown.                                                                                          | `false`                |
| `hideInBulk`           | `boolean`                             | Suppress in the bulk toolbar. Implicit when no `onMulti` is provided.                                                      | `false`                |
| `rowVisible`           | `(item) => boolean`                   | Per-row predicate for the row dropdown. Hide actions the row isn't eligible for.                                           | —                      |
| `onSingle`             | `(item) => void \| Promise<void>`     | Row-dropdown handler. Receives the full row.                                                                                | —                      |
| `onMulti`              | `(ids) => void \| Promise<void>`      | Bulk-toolbar handler. Receives selected IDs.                                                                                | —                      |
| `refreshAfter`         | `boolean`                             | Call `dataSource.refresh()` after the handler resolves.                                                                     | `true`                 |
| `clearSelectionAfter`  | `boolean`                             | Wipe the selection after the handler resolves.                                                                              | `true` bulk / `false` single |

## Selection options

`SelectionOptions` is for fine-tuning when the defaults aren't right.

```typescript
const config: DataTableConfig<UserData> = {
    // ...
    selection: {
        enabled: true,                                    // force the checkbox column on without actions
        selectableRows: (item) => item.role !== 'admin',  // disable selection per row
        hideRowActionsColumn: false,                      // hide the trailing three-dot column
        primaryActionsCount: 2                            // cap primary buttons before overflow
    }
};
```

| Property              | Type               | Description                                                                                                  | Default     |
|:----------------------|:-------------------|:-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|:------------|
| `enabled`             | `boolean`          | Force the selection column on even without actions. Useful when binding `selectedIds` for a custom UI.        | `actions.length > 0` |
| `selectableRows`      | `(item) => boolean`| Per-row gate. `false` renders a disabled checkbox.                                                            | all selectable |
| `hideRowActionsColumn`| `boolean`          | Hide the trailing per-row dropdown. Useful when actions should only fire from the bulk toolbar.               | `false`     |
| `primaryActionsCount` | `number`           | Maximum `primary: true` actions rendered as buttons in the toolbar. Surplus falls into the "More" overflow.   | `2`         |

## Two-way binding

Bind `selectedIds` to drive selection from outside (default selections, persistence, custom toolbars):

```svelte
<DataTable
    {config}
    {dataSource}
    bind:selectedIds
    onSelectionChange={({ ids, loadedItems }) => {
        // loadedItems is the subset currently rendered — cross-page IDs aren't in here
    }}
/>
```

Both `bind:selectedIds` and `onSelectionChange` fire on every change; pick whichever fits — they're not mutually exclusive.

